{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"_kritt_extractor_helper\": true,\n  \"stub\": false,\n  \"stub_explanation\": \"\",\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"flow_summary\": \"Successfully refunds 1–100 distinct caller-owned tickets in Refunding status. Burns the tickets, reduces the refund liability, transfers their full entry value to the caller, emits TicketsRefunded, and returns the amount.\",\n      \"flow_trace\": [\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:349 Raffle.refundTickets - receives the ABI-decoded ordered uint256[] ticketIds in the clone's execution context.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:69 nonReentrant - checks that the guard is not entered and marks it entered for the entire refund.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:350 Raffle.refundTickets - requires Status.Refunding through _requireStatus at line 573.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:351 Raffle.refundTickets - accepts only 1–100 ticket IDs; MAX_REFUND_TICKET_BATCH_SIZE is defined at RaffleConstants.sol:27.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:357 Raffle.refundTickets - processes IDs in submitted order; ownerOf must find a live ticket, and its current owner must equal msg.sender.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:451 Raffle.ticketRange - reads the selected ticket's stored inclusive firstEntry and lastEntry.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:363 Raffle.refundTickets - adds lastEntry - firstEntry + 1 to aggregateEntries and calls _burn(ticketId).\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:303 ERC721._burn - dispatches to _update with zero recipient and zero authorization argument; authorization was already enforced by refundTickets.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:497 Raffle._update - allows the zero-address burn and delegates to ERC721._update.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:216 ERC721._update - clears the ticket approval, decrements the owner's ticket balance, sets ownership to zero, and emits Transfer; the historical ticket range remains stored.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:367 Raffle.refundTickets - computes amount = aggregateEntries * ENTRY_PRICE, where ENTRY_PRICE is 1,000,000 raw quote-token units, then subtracts amount from remainingRefundLiability.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:564 Raffle._transferQuote - screens msg.sender as the payout destination before transferring.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:593 Raffle._isProtocolDestination - checks fixed protocol addresses, queries the immutable factory's raffleImplementation getter, and additionally queries isRaffle(msg.sender) when the recipient has code; these getters are declared at RaffleFactory.sol:42 and RaffleFactory.sol:54.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/utils/SafeERC20.sol:33 SafeERC20.safeTransfer - receives the immutable quoteToken, caller-derived destination, and computed amount.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/utils/SafeERC20.sol:176 SafeERC20._safeTransfer - encodes transfer(to, amount), calls the quote token at line 184, and validates success; accepts a true return word or a successful empty return from an address with code.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:370 Raffle.refundTickets - reads the remaining liability and emits TicketsRefunded(msg.sender, ticketQuantity, aggregateEntries, amount, liabilityAfter).\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:102 _nonReentrantAfter - releases the guard; refundTickets returns the named uint256 amount.\"\n      ],\n      \"flow_terminal_action\": \"Commit the ticket burns and liability reduction, pay the caller through the configured quote token, emit TicketsRefunded, and return amount.\",\n      \"flow_file_path\": \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\n      \"flow_line\": 369,\n      \"flow_input_to_sink\": \"The ordered ticket IDs select live tickets and their stored entry ranges. Their aggregate entry count determines the transfer amount; msg.sender determines the recipient. The caller cannot supply a separate payout address, token address, or refund value.\",\n      \"flow_security_relevance\": \"This is the asset-release boundary. Review current-owner authorization, consumption of each bearer claim, entry-value calculation, liability reduction before the external transfer, and atomic completion. Contract recipients receive the same ERC20 payout without a recipient callback or asynchronous continuation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"flow_summary\": \"Rejects a nested refund invocation while another nonReentrant operation on the same raffle is executing, before checking lifecycle or ticket IDs.\",\n      \"flow_trace\": [\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:349 Raffle.refundTickets - receives a nested call with an ABI-decoded ticket array; this is reachable when an owner contract calls during the buyEntries receiver callback initiated at Raffle.sol:235.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:69 nonReentrant - invokes _nonReentrantBefore.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:94 _nonReentrantBefore - checks the existing guard state through _nonReentrantBeforeView.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:88 _nonReentrantBeforeView - detects the entered guard and reverts ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall.\"\n      ],\n      \"flow_terminal_action\": \"Revert the nested invocation with ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall before executing the refund body.\",\n      \"flow_file_path\": \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol\",\n      \"flow_line\": 90,\n      \"flow_input_to_sink\": \"The caller's entire ticketIds array reaches the guarded entrypoint but no ticket element is inspected.\",\n      \"flow_security_relevance\": \"This boundary prevents nested claim processing across guarded raffle operations. Its reachability comes from an existing guarded operation's callback; the normal refund payout does not invoke a callback on the ticket owner.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"flow_summary\": \"Rejects a refund when the raffle is not in Refunding status.\",\n      \"flow_trace\": [\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:349 Raffle.refundTickets - receives the ABI-decoded ticketIds array.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:94 _nonReentrantBefore - passes the reentrancy check and enters the guard.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:350 Raffle.refundTickets - invokes _requireStatus(Status.Refunding) before inspecting array length or ownership.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:573 Raffle._requireStatus - detects a different lifecycle status and reverts InvalidStatus(status).\"\n      ],\n      \"flow_terminal_action\": \"Revert with InvalidStatus(actualStatus), leaving tickets, balances, and refund accounting unchanged.\",\n      \"flow_file_path\": \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\n      \"flow_line\": 574,\n      \"flow_input_to_sink\": \"Any submitted ticketIds array reaches this lifecycle check; its contents cannot override the stored status.\",\n      \"flow_security_relevance\": \"This gate separates full refunds from active sales, pending draws, and resolved winner outcomes. Expiration alone does not make this entrypoint enable refunds.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"flow_summary\": \"Rejects an empty batch or a batch containing more than 100 ticket IDs before processing any ticket.\",\n      \"flow_trace\": [\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:349 Raffle.refundTickets - receives the ABI-decoded ticketIds array and passes the nonReentrant guard.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:350 Raffle.refundTickets - confirms Status.Refunding.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:351 Raffle.refundTickets - reads ticketIds.length into ticketQuantity.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/libraries/RaffleConstants.sol:27 RaffleConstants.MAX_REFUND_TICKET_BATCH_SIZE - supplies the limit of 100 tickets.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:352 Raffle.refundTickets - detects ticketQuantity == 0 or ticketQuantity > 100 and reverts InvalidTicketBatchSize(ticketQuantity, 100).\"\n      ],\n      \"flow_terminal_action\": \"Revert with InvalidTicketBatchSize without reading ticket ownership, burning tickets, or transferring funds.\",\n      \"flow_file_path\": \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\n      \"flow_line\": 353,\n      \"flow_input_to_sink\": \"The externally controlled array length becomes the rejected quantity in the custom error; individual IDs are not examined.\",\n      \"flow_security_relevance\": \"This validation bounds the ticket-processing loop and rejects empty refund operations. The limit applies to ticket count, while each ticket can represent multiple entries.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"flow_summary\": \"Rejects a batch containing a live ticket owned by someone other than the caller, including when the caller has ERC721 approval. Any earlier burns in the batch are rolled back.\",\n      \"flow_trace\": [\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:349 Raffle.refundTickets - receives ticketIds and passes the nonReentrant guard.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:350 Raffle.refundTickets - requires Refunding status and a batch length of 1–100.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:357 Raffle.refundTickets - processes IDs in order; any preceding caller-owned tickets have their entry ranges counted and are provisionally burned.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:359 Raffle.refundTickets - calls ownerOf for the offending ticket ID.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:61 ERC721.ownerOf - uses _requireOwned at line 426 to return the live ticket's current owner.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:360 Raffle.refundTickets - finds msg.sender != owner and reverts NotTicketOwner(ticketId, msg.sender, owner).\"\n      ],\n      \"flow_terminal_action\": \"Revert with NotTicketOwner and roll back all earlier ticket burns and logs from this refund invocation.\",\n      \"flow_file_path\": \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\n      \"flow_line\": 360,\n      \"flow_input_to_sink\": \"The selected offending ticket ID is compared against its stored owner, and the ID, caller, and actual owner are included in the error.\",\n      \"flow_security_relevance\": \"Refund authorization requires the current owner directly. Token-specific approvals and operator approvals do not authorize payment to an operator; a mixed-ownership batch cannot partially execute.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"flow_summary\": \"Rejects an ID that was never minted or was already burned before this invocation. Stored historical ranges do not allow a consumed claim to be refunded again.\",\n      \"flow_trace\": [\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:349 Raffle.refundTickets - receives ticketIds and passes the nonReentrant guard.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:350 Raffle.refundTickets - confirms Refunding status and an accepted batch length.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:357 Raffle.refundTickets - processes any preceding valid IDs, then selects the nonexistent or previously burned ID.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:359 Raffle.refundTickets - calls ownerOf before reading the selected ticket's range.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:61 ERC721.ownerOf - delegates existence validation to _requireOwned.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:426 ERC721._requireOwned - reads zero ownership and reverts ERC721NonexistentToken(tokenId) at line 429.\"\n      ],\n      \"flow_terminal_action\": \"Revert with ERC721NonexistentToken, rolling back any preceding burns; no refund transfer occurs.\",\n      \"flow_file_path\": \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol\",\n      \"flow_line\": 429,\n      \"flow_input_to_sink\": \"The caller-selected invalid ID indexes the ownership mapping and becomes the tokenId in the custom error.\",\n      \"flow_security_relevance\": \"Existence validation precedes range aggregation, preventing nonexistent tickets and retained historical ranges from becoming payable claims.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"flow_summary\": \"Rejects a duplicate ID within an otherwise valid batch because its first occurrence burns the ticket before the repeated occurrence is checked.\",\n      \"flow_trace\": [\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:349 Raffle.refundTickets - receives an ordered array containing a repeated caller-owned ticket ID and passes the nonReentrant guard.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:350 Raffle.refundTickets - confirms Refunding status and a batch length of 1–100.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:359 Raffle.refundTickets - verifies that the first occurrence exists and is owned by msg.sender.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:362 Raffle.refundTickets - reads the first occurrence's stored range, adds its entry count, and calls _burn at line 364.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:303 ERC721._burn - routes through Raffle._update at Raffle.sol:497 into ERC721._update.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:240 ERC721._update - sets the first occurrence's owner to address(0) and emits its provisional burn event.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:357 Raffle.refundTickets - later reaches the repeated ID and calls ownerOf again at line 359.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:426 ERC721._requireOwned - observes the zero owner created earlier in this invocation and reverts ERC721NonexistentToken at line 429.\"\n      ],\n      \"flow_terminal_action\": \"Revert the entire batch, restoring the first occurrence and every other provisionally burned ticket; no transfer occurs.\",\n      \"flow_file_path\": \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\n      \"flow_line\": 364,\n      \"flow_input_to_sink\": \"Repeated values in the ordered array address the same ownership slot. The first occurrence clears it, causing the later occurrence to fail before its entries can be counted again.\",\n      \"flow_security_relevance\": \"Sequential ownership consumption provides duplicate rejection without a separate deduplication structure. Review the ordering of existence checks, aggregation, and burns together with transaction rollback.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"flow_summary\": \"A valid batch reaches the external quote-token transfer, but a rejected transfer causes the entire refund to revert, restoring ticket ownership and refund liability.\",\n      \"flow_trace\": [\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:349 Raffle.refundTickets - receives ticketIds and passes the nonReentrant guard.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:350 Raffle.refundTickets - validates Refunding status, the 1–100 batch limit, and caller ownership of every selected ticket.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:362 Raffle.refundTickets - aggregates stored entry ranges and burns each ticket through ERC721._burn and the Raffle._update override.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:367 Raffle.refundTickets - computes the full entry-value refun